        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "9a0a8146082e000d8f2c4db646573be61727813d",
            "parents": [
                "e5cafef0032e7b7e93624ea8642f06a56b14bf35"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/92/91892/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "mahalakshmik-1",
                "email": "mahalakshmik@ami.com",
                "username": "mahalakshmik-1"
            },
            "createdOn": 1782888570,
            "author": {
                "name": "mahalakshmik-1",
                "email": "mahalakshmik@ami.com",
                "username": "mahalakshmik-1"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "my query:\n\nWho is expected to consume this signal?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mahalakshmik-1",
                        "email": "mahalakshmik@ami.com",
                        "username": "mahalakshmik-1"
                    },
                    "message": "Expected consumers are D-Bus clients that only need binary running\nstate and want normal property reads plus PropertiesChanged on the same\nfan_tach object, instead of deriving from floating-point RPM."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Who is expected to consume this signal?\n\nsorry, i did not write it clearly.\n\nWhich specific upstream repositories or upstream services will consume this signal?\n\n\nin my humble opinion, let's not merge any D-Bus interfaces based on a hypothetical possible future usage but rather on a concrete need with at least WIP / PoC implementation of both the producer and consumer (end-to-end testing)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mahalakshmik-1",
                        "email": "mahalakshmik@ami.com",
                        "username": "mahalakshmik-1"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the clarification. This is now backed by a concrete consumer, not a hypothetical one.\nIn phosphor-pid-control, DbusPassive now consumes xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.FanStatus.Running from PropertiesChanged on the same fan tach object path and uses it for fan fail-safe decisions.\nSo, this interface is now producer + consumer validated end-to-end (dbus-sensors produces Running, phosphor-pid-control consumes it)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/FanStatus.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Would this be the fan_tach sensor object or something else?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/FanStatus.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mahalakshmik-1",
                        "email": "mahalakshmik@ami.com",
                        "username": "mahalakshmik-1"
                    },
                    "message": "Implemented on the same fan_tach sensor object as Sensor.Value, not a\nseparate object. FanStatus is now explicitly documented and implemented\non /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/fan_tach/<name>."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/FanStatus.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Why a signal and not a property - also see next comment."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/FanStatus.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mahalakshmik-1",
                        "email": "mahalakshmik@ami.com",
                        "username": "mahalakshmik-1"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed. I changed from FanRunning signal to Running property in\nSensor.FanStatus. This follows normal OpenBMC D-Bus modeling and uses\nstandard PropertiesChanged updates."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/FanStatus.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "If this is based on fan RPM, isn't that part of another property/sensor already which users can determine based on property changes?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/FanStatus.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mahalakshmik-1",
                        "email": "mahalakshmik@ami.com",
                        "username": "mahalakshmik-1"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree that Running is derived from RPM > 0. The goal is to standardize\nthat derived binary state in one producer-side property so clients do\nnot duplicate RPM parsing and transition logic."
                }
            ],
